public","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/12852722-S.jpg","details":{"works":[{"key":"/works/OL28602228W"}],"title":"Catholic Republic","publishers":["Sophia Institute Press"],"publish_date":"April 18, 2019","key":"/books/OL39216089M","type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"identifiers":{},"covers":[12852722],"isbn_13":["9781622828364"],"isbn_10":["1622828364"],"classifications":{},"weight":"14.4 ounces","number_of_pages":304,"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"copyright_date":"2019","subtitle":"Why America Will Perish Without Rome","edition_name":"1st Edition","publish_places":["USA"],"physical_format":"Paperback","latest_revision":3,"revision":3,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2022-08-05T00:42:44.635564"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2022-08-05T00:46:33.037049"}}},"ISBN:9781558761346":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9781558761346","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL8608095M/Shi'a_Islam","preview":"borrow","preview_url":"https://archive.org/details/shiaislamfromrel0000halm","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/1882453-S.jpg","details":{"publishers":["Markus Wiener Publishers"],"number_of_pages":176,"subtitle":"From Religion to Revolution (Princeton Series on the Middle East)","weight":"15.2 ounces","isbn_10":["1558761349"],"covers":[1882453],"physical_format":"Hardcover","lc_classifications":["BP192 .H3513 1997","BP192.H3513 1996","BP192 .H3513 1996"],"key":"/books/OL8608095M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL439802A","name":"Heinz Halm"},{"key":"/authors/OL3040072A","name":"Allison Brown"}],"ocaid":"shiaislamfromrel0000halm","languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"source_records":["ia:shiaislamfromrel0000halm","marc:marc_loc_2016/BooksAll.2016.part25.utf8:100859050:904","bwb:9781558761346","marc:marc_nuls/NULS_PHC_180925.mrc:47502351:1189","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-004.mrc:544991825:4801","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_005.bib.mrc:200057138:5189"],"title":"Shi'a Islam","lccn":["96035459"],"identifiers":{"goodreads":["4342525"]},"isbn_13":["9781558761346"],"edition_name":"New Ed edition","subjects":["Cultural studies","History of religion","Islam","Islamic studies","Shiah","Religion","Shåi°ah","Islam - Shi'a","Islam - General","History"],"publish_date":"November 1996","works":[{"key":"/works/OL2894311W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"physical_dimensions":"8.9 x 6 x 0.8 inches","local_id":["urn:nuls:31786102059299"],"oclc_numbers":["35650912"],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"The author highlights the three main aspects of Shi'a Islam: its historical development, especially the history of the Imams; the rituals, including flagellation and passion plays; and the rule of the mullahs, known as the \"government of experts.\".\n\nShi'ism is as old as Islam. It began as an exclusively Arab political issue of succession to Muhammad, and was later embraced by the Iranians. At the core of Shi'i religious practice are rituals of mourning and atonement. Halm describes the elegies of mourning and the ta'ziye (passion plays) and includes travelers' accounts over the course of several centuries that establish striking similarities between Iranian and particular Christian practices.\n\nHalm explains the exalted position of the religious scholars, the mullahs and ayatollahs, who established themselves as clergy in the Safavid empire and defined themselves as \"administrators\" for the Hidden Imam. Their authority is based on idtschtihad, the rational interpretation of the Koran and the traditions of the Imans. The relationship between the rulers of Iran and the mullahs has always been tense. The Khomeini revolution was the powerful culmination of a lengthy history of conflict."},"latest_revision":11,"revision":11,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-30T08:14:56.482104"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2025-06-20T11:15:32.157830"}}},"ISBN:9781558761353":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9781558761353","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL8608096M/Shi'a_Islam","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL8608096M/Shi'a_Islam","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/785514-S.jpg","details":{"identifiers":{"librarything":["1623982"],"goodreads":["932466"]},"title":"Shi'a Islam","subtitle":"From Religion to Revolution (Princeton Series on the Middle East)","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL439802A","name":"Heinz Halm"},{"key":"/authors/OL3040072A","name":"Allison Brown"}],"publish_date":"November 1996","publishers":["Markus Wiener Publishers"],"weight":"10.4 ounces","covers":[785514],"physical_format":"Paperback","subjects":["Cultural studies","History of religion","Islam","Islamic studies","Religion - World Religions","Islam - General","Religion","Shiah","Comparative Religion","Islam - Shi'a","History","Shåi°ah"],"isbn_13":["9781558761353"],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"isbn_10":["1558761357"],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"physical_dimensions":"8.9 x 5.9 x 0.6 inches","source_records":["amazon:1558761357"],"key":"/books/OL8608096M","number_of_pages":176,"works":[{"key":"/works/OL2894311W"}],"latest_revision":7,"revision":7,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-30T08:14:56.482104"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2025-12-28T18:09:35.378329"}}},"ISBN:9780195138757":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9780195138757","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL6787349M/Teaching_spirits","preview":"restricted","preview_url":"https://archive.org/details/teachingspiritsu00brow","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/125132-S.jpg","details":{"publishers":["Oxford University Press"],"identifiers":{"librarything":["907089"],"goodreads":["1263521"]},"subtitle":"understanding Native American religious traditions","isbn_10":["0195138759"],"subject_place":["North America."],"covers":[125132],"lc_classifications":["E98.R3 B753 2001","E98.R3B753 2001"],"key":"/books/OL6787349M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL389248A","name":"Joseph Epes Brown"}],"ocaid":"teachingspiritsu00brow","publish_places":["Oxford, [England]","New York"],"contributions":["Cousins, Emily, 1969-"],"subjects":["Indians of North America -- Religion","Indian mythology -- North America","Indians of North America -- Rites and ceremonies"],"pagination":"xxiii, 140 p. :","source_records":["marc:marc_records_scriblio_net/part01.dat:12215286:908","marc:marc_loc_updates/v35.i21.records.utf8:162181:1125","marc:marc_ithaca_college/ic_marc.mrc:181841681:1005","ia:teachingspiritsu00brow","amazon:0195138759","marc:marc_marygrove/marygrovecollegelibrary.full.D20191108.T213022.internetarchive2nd_REPACK.mrc:140315272:5330","marc:marc_claremont_school_theology/CSTMARC2_barcode.mrc:14103860:5607","marc:marc_loc_2016/BooksAll.2016.part01.utf8:27776090:1125","bwb:9780195138757","marc:marc_claremont_school_theology/CSTMARC2_multibarcode.mrc:14110891:5607","ia:teachingspiritsu0000brow","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-010.mrc:35256180:1420","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-007.mrc:76078047:1381","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_019.bib.mrc:62393055:3732"],"title":"Teaching spirits","dewey_decimal_class":["299/.7"],"notes":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Includes bibliographical references (p. [127]-132) and index."},"number_of_pages":140,"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"lccn":["00044072"],"local_id":["urn:mgc:31927000901469","urn:cst:10017047424"],"publish_date":"2001","publish_country":"enk","by_statement":"Joseph Epes Brown with Emily Cousins.","works":[{"key":"/works/OL2668270W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"oclc_numbers":["44270337"],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Publisher description: Teaching Spirits offers a thematic approach to Native American religious traditions. Within the great multiplicity of Native American cultures, Joseph Epes Brown has perceived certain common themes that resonate within many Native traditions. He demonstrates how themes within native traditions connect with each other, at the same time upholding the integrity of individual traditions. Brown illustrates each of these themes with in-depth explorations of specific native cultures including Lakota, Navajo, Apache, Koyukon, and Ojibwe. Brown demonstrates how Native American values provide an alternative metaphysics that stand opposed to modern materialism. He shows how these spiritual values provide material for a serious rethinking of modern attitudes - especially toward the environment - as well as how they may help non-native peoples develop a more sensitive response to native concerns. Throughout, he draws on his extensive personal experience with Black Elk, who came to symbolize for many the greatness of the imperiled native cultures."},"latest_revision":21,"revision":21,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-01T03:28:50.625462"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2025-10-17T01:14:28.817401"}}},"ISBN:9780195350081":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9780195350081","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL35890506M/Teaching_Spirits","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL35890506M/Teaching_Spirits","details":{"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL389248A","name":"Joseph Epes Brown"},{"key":"/authors/OL301488A","name":"Emily Cousins"}],"isbn_13":["9780195350081"],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"publish_date":"2001","publishers":["Oxford University Press, Incorporated"],"source_records":["bwb:9780195350081"],"title":"Teaching Spirits","subtitle":"Understanding Native American Religious Traditions","full_title":"Teaching Spirits Understanding Native American Religious Traditions","works":[{"key":"/works/OL2668270W"}],"key":"/books/OL35890506M","latest_revision":1,"revision":1,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2021-12-26T16:32:45.356349"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2021-12-26T16:32:45.356349"}}},"ISBN:9781280531033":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9781280531033","info_url":"http://ope